# GBO — environment variables
#
# IMPORTANT: this file MUST live at the repo root (same folder as this
# file, next to database.py/supabase_client.py/r2_client.py) — NOT
# inside shiny_app/. python-dotenv looks for .env starting from the
# directory of the file that calls load_dotenv() (database.py,
# supabase_client.py, r2_client.py — all at the repo root) and walks
# UP the directory tree, never down into subfolders. An .env placed in
# shiny_app/ is silently never read, no matter which command you run
# it with.
#
# Setup:
#   1. cp .env.example .env      (from the repo root)
#   2. Fill in the real values below (get them from supabase.com and,
#      for the R2_* ones, from the Cloudflare dashboard — see
#      r2_client.py's docstring for exact steps).
#   3. Never commit .env — it's already in .gitignore.

# --- Required to start the app at all -------------------------------
# Supabase -> Settings -> Database -> Connection string (URI, "Session" mode)
DATABASE_URL=

# Supabase -> Settings -> API
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Optional: only needed for video upload (R2 storage) features ---
# Cloudflare dashboard -> R2 -> Manage API Tokens
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
R2_BUCKET_NAME=
R2_PUBLIC_URL_BASE=
